  "title": "Tipu Sultan",
  "summary": "Tipu Sultan ruled Mysore from 1782 until 1799, succeeding his father Haydar Ali, and fought the East India Company in the Mysore Wars. EBSCO records that he fell in a British assault on his capital Seringapatam on 4 May 1799, after which the Company decided against annexing Mysore. The V&A explains the tiger motif of his court through the name Haidar.",
